// - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
// Filename:	AS LED Driver PCB0.6.test
// Project:		VSC80,800,900,90
// Author:      Foster & Freeman Ltd - Paul Evans
// Modified:    29/07/24
//
// Description: Using the nano inside TE209 to control the relay (x2) for 5V regulator  to the PICKkit4 and the power on button.
// Check current fw and if not expect updates the fw. 
// Steps 3 to 4.6 are setup/logic for the test box itself
// Tests the Driver with a constance resistance using the TEMMA Programmable load.
// the PCB Dept PSU is limited tp 3A so the code has been ajusted to work within this limit.
// 15 LEDS per bank = 37.5V, CR = 11.20ohms, Current is approx 1A ( PCB to work upto 1A)
//
// - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -

[0] force FAIL by default to avoid IMPORTANT message below.
#1: Enter operator initials and PCB serial number:
a. Enter operator intials.
b. Enter serial number into the box below.
IMPORTANT: Observe ESD precautions for handling ESD sensitive devices. 
DISPLAY: 260-038-CP-00.png
CLICK_OK: 


#2: Equipment Setup 1
a. Connect the PSU to the VSC90 Controller Test Box(TE209).
b. Connect the PC (via USB) to K5 on the VSC90 Controller Test Box(TE209).
c. Connect the PC (via USB) to the TENMA Programmable Load.
d. Connect the PC (via USB) to the TENMA Programmable PSU.
DISPLAY: ASsetup.png
COMMENT: *Example image below*
CLICK_OK:


#3: Equipment Setup 2
a. Connect the UUT to the Test box (TE209).
b. Connect the COAX PCB to the J3 on the UUT.
c. Place the UUT inside the LED Test Box with Web Camera (TE086).
d. Set the TENMA Programmable PSU power switch to on.
CLICK_OK:

#3.1: Connect to the Nano
CONNECT: TE209				// Connect to the Nano in the TE209
IF_NOT:
GOTO: #3.1: 
COMMAND: TE209 OUT RC7 1 	// TURN Power button RELAY OFF
COMMAND: TE209 OUT RC6 1 	// TURN Pickit RELAY OFF

#3.2: Connect to the PSU
CONNECT: TENMAPSU
IF_NOT:
GOTO: #3.2: 

#4: Configure the PSU
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUT0
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OCP1
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OCPSET1:500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET1:12.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET1:1.500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH1:1

#4.1: Power on the test box.
COMMAND: TE209 OUT RC7 0 		// TURN power button RELAY ON
DELAY: 500
COMMAND: TE209 OUT RC7 1 		// TURN power button RELAY OFF
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned voltage is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.060 0.015 // Set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
IF: 							// True result, current is good
GOTO: #4.2: 
IMPORTANT: This test has failed, check the power button has been pressed, power supply, USB connection and the ftdi chip.		
PASS_FAIL: #4.1:


#4.2: Connect to the test box
a. If error message below is diplayed, then click OK to continue. 
.
ERROR on line 71, CONNECT_ VSC90 - Not available.
DELAY: 9000 					// GIVE TIME FOR THE PC AND NEW ftdi TO WAKE
CONNECT: VSC90	 				// Test connection to the FDTI chip
IF_NOT: 						// If wrong FTDI porgram
GOTO: #4.3: 					// Reprogram the FTDI and PIC
GOTO: #4.6: 					// FTDI is correct now check the PIC is programmed correctly 


#4.3: program the FTDI 
EXE: ftdi_programmer_vsc90.exe
#4.3.1: program the PIC
COMMAND: TE209 OUT RC6 0 		// TURN PICKIT RELAY ON
EXE: VSC90FWself_powered.bat
DELAY: 2000
COMMAND: TE209 OUT RC6 1 		// TURN PICKIT RELAY OFF
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH1:0
DELAY: 2000
GOTO: #4.4: // 

#4.3.2: program the PIC attempt 2 
DISCONNECT: VSC90
COMMAND: TE209 OUT RC6 0 		// TURN PICKIT RELAY ON
EXE: VSC90FWself_powered.bat
DELAY: 2000
COMMAND: TE209 OUT RC6 1 		// TURN PICKIT RELAY OFF
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH1:0
DELAY: 2000

#4.4:  Press the I/O Power button and turn on the test box
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH1:1
COMMAND: TE209 OUT RC7 0 		// TURN power button RELAY ON
DELAY: 500
COMMAND: TE209 OUT RC7 1 		// TURN power button RELAY OFF
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned voltage is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.060 0.015 // Set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 				
IF_NOT: 
GOTO: #4.4: 					// There is fault with the current reading, go back and try again 

#4.5: Connect again
DELAY: 7000 					// GIVE TIME FOR THE pc AND NEW ftdi TO WAKE
CONNECT: VSC90
IF_NOT: 
GOTO: #4: 						// GO BACK TO THE START

#4.6: PCB Program version check.
COMMAND: VSC90  TYPE 			// Check connection to the PIC chip
READLINE: VSC90  TYPE
Returned product is = %TYPE%
[%TYPE% STR_EQ VSC90] 			// Evaluates the FW by checking inside the [] and set true or false flag
IF:
GOTO: #5: 						// Checks and programming complete goto the start of tests
ELSE: 							// PIC is not programmed correctly still
IMPORTANT: Cannot program the test box (PIC). Please check connections to the PIC Kit and PCB.
CLICK_OK:
GOTO: #4.3.2: 					// Try programming the PIC again


#5: Configure the TENMA Programmable Load 
CONNECT: TENMALOAD
IF_NOT:
GOTO: #2:
COMMAND: TENMALOAD :INPut OFF
COMMAND: TENMALOAD :FUNC RES
COMMAND: TENMALOAD :RESistance 11.2OHM
COMMAND: TENMALOAD :INPut ON


#6: Set to the test box to drive the bank AS1 
COMMAND: VSC90 AS0
COMMAND: VSC90 AS1
COMMAND: VSC90 ASHIGH


#7: Read the current from the TEMMALOAD and evaluate current for PASS or FAIL.
DELAY: 5000 
COMMAND: TENMALOAD :MEAS:CURR?
READLINE: TENMALOAD TEMMAcurrent
The returned voltage is =  %TEMMAcurrent%
RANGE: %TEMMAcurrent% 1.0000 0.05 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail


#8: Set to the test box to drive the AS2 bank
COMMAND: VSC90 AS0
COMMAND: VSC90 AS2
COMMAND: VSC90 ASHIGH

#9: Read the current from the TEMMALOAD and evaluate the current for PASS or FAIL.
DELAY: 5000
COMMAND: TENMALOAD :MEAS:CURR?
READLINE: TENMALOAD TEMMAcurrent
The returned voltage is =  %TEMMAcurrent%
RANGE: %TEMMAcurrent% 1.0000 0.05						
SUB: TestPassOrFail


#10: Test complete
COMMAND: VSC90 If#	// turn off any LEDs still on: 
COMMAND: VSC90 AS0
COMMAND: TENMALOAD :RESistance 0OHM
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET1:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET1:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUT0
COMMAND: VSC90 AS0
IF: %FAILED% > 0
GOTO: #Failed:
ELSE: #Passed:


#Failed: A test failed
a. This PCB has failed to pass all Tests
b. Check the Log file for more details on the failed test(s).
IMPORTANT: This PCB has failed to pass all Tests
DISPLAY: test_failed.png
CLICK_OK:
GOTO: #QUIT:

#Passed: Test's Complete
a. All tests instructions have been completed and a log file created.
b. Click OK to finish and power OFF.
DISPLAY: AllTestsPassed.png
CLICK_OK:

#QUIT:
COMMAND: VSC90 AS0
COMMAND: TENMALOAD :INPut OFF
COMMAND: TENMALOAD :RESistance 0OHM
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET1:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET1:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUT0
DISCONNECT: TENMAPSU
DISCONNECT: TE209
DISCONNECT: VSC90
// End of file
// - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -